Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Jiggles">Jiggles</a>&nbsp;(---.roleplayers.org)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;03-06-01 01:08<br>
<br><HTML>Here's a quickie for how I've gotten to @55 so far.  This should take you to 80.<br>
<br>
1-15: Silk Thread: make silk thread by combining two spiderling silks together.<br>
<br>
15-26: Patchwork armor: take one pattern and a ruined pelt<br>
<br>
26-31: Leather padding: Go hunting in East and West commons for pelts.  Look for LQ pelts and combine one with a silk thread to make leather padding til 31.  I will personally buy stacks of leather padding for 50pp.  If you want, you can find a smith and have them make you a skinning knife.  By combining a skinning knife with a MQ or HQ pelt it will drop it down one notch.  Only to be used on wolf/cat/bear pelts not lion, puma, etc.<br>
<br>
31-56: Studded Leather Masks: find a smith to make you a few stacks of studs.  take one stud, a MQ pelt, and a mask pattern (bought in north ro)<br>
<br>
56-82: Cured silk Armor: find a brewer and have them make you a few stacks of heady kiola.  Take one mask pattern, one heady kiola, and one silk swatch (SWATCH, not thread.. swatches are made from two spider silks, not spiderling)<br>
<br>
82-108: Reinforced Leather Armor:  find a smith again and have them make you a few stacks of steel boning.  Take one boning, a mask pattern, and a HQ pelt and combine.<br>
<br>
After 108, you either have to do cultural tailoring as a wood elf or halfling, OR attempt the new Velium tailoring.  Good luck, as this stuff is trival over 200 with no step between really.  So you'll fail alot, and its expensive.<br>
<br>
Again, check out http://www.eqtraders.com.<br>
<br>
-Jiggs</HTML></font></tt><p>
